// Focused view: Identity service with its direct neighbors only.

views {
  style element.tag = #frontend   { color blue }
  style element.tag = #backend    { color sky }
  style element.tag = #data       { color secondary }
  style element.tag = #adminPlane { color indigo }
  style element.tag = #federation { color green }

  view serviceIdentity of velox.identityService {
    title "Services / Identity"
    description '''
      Auth gate, key vault, KeyPackage directory, and (via Federation Edge) the
      federation-facing user directory. Verifies credentials, runs the KEK challenge,
      issues JWTs, returns passphrase-wrapped encryption keys, publishes local users'
      MLS KeyPackages to peer instances, and owns per-user consent for remote
      first-contact.

      Federation endpoints served through Federation Edge (WIP — draft-ietf-mimi-protocol):
        - `/keyMaterial/{user}`       — local users' KeyPackages (single-use, pre-published)
        - `/identifierQuery/{domain}` — user directory search (scoped by searchability policy)
        - `/requestConsent`           — inbound consent request from a remote user
        - `/updateConsent`            — inbound notification of a consent decision from a peer

      ---

      **KEK (Key Encryption Key)** — Derived client-side from the user's passphrase via a
      memory-hard KDF (e.g. Argon2). The client signs a server-issued nonce with the KEK to
      prove key ownership without ever transmitting the KEK itself.

      **Passphrase-wrapped key** — The real MLS encryption key, encrypted with the KEK.
      Stored server-side in Identity Postgres. Decrypted locally after a successful KEK challenge.

      **Challenge nonce** — A random value issued by Identity at login start. The client
      derives the KEK, signs the nonce, and returns the signature. Identity verifies the
      signature to confirm the client knows the correct passphrase — without storing the KEK.

      **JWT (JSON Web Token)** — Signed bearer token issued after successful authentication.
      Services validate it independently without calling Identity on every request.

      **OTP (One-Time Password)** — Optional second factor (e.g. TOTP via RFC 6238).
      Verified by Identity alongside the password hash before issuing the JWT.

      **OIDC (OpenID Connect)** — Optional external IdP path. Identity federates to the
      external provider but still enforces a local KEK challenge before granting access.

      **KeyPackage** — Pre-published signed bundle (RFC 9420) containing a user's client
      credential + HPKE public key. Single-use; consumed when a user is added to an MLS group.

      **AS (Authentication Service)** — RFC 9420 §5.3.1 concept. Identity is the AS for LOCAL
      users; remote-user credentials are validated client-side by checking the peer instance's
      ed25519 signature on the federation response plus the KeyPackage self-signature.

      **Consent (WIP)** — MIMI requires explicit recipient consent before a peer can fetch
      a user's KeyPackage. Identity stores the decision per (local-user, remote-domain-or-user)
      and enforces it on every inbound `/keyMaterial` request. Tracks draft-ietf-mimi-protocol;
      both the spec and the Velox implementation are work-in-progress.
    '''
    include *
    include -> velox.identityService ->
    autoLayout LeftRight 120 80
  }
}
